---
import ThemeSwitcher from "../components/ThemeSwitcher.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <div
    class="mx-auto mt-8 grid max-w-screen-lg grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-12"
  >
    <div class="typeset col-span-2 flex min-w-full flex-col">
      <div
        class="flex w-full flex-row items-end justify-around gap-2 md:ml-auto"
      >
        <ThemeSwitcher />
        <p class="font-serif">Colophon</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div
    class="mx-auto mt-4 grid max-w-screen-lg grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-12"
  >
    <div class="col-span-2 flex min-w-full flex-col">
      <div class="flex flex-row items-end gap-2 md:ml-auto">
        <p class="text-muted-foreground font-serif">Tech</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-span-8 min-w-full rounded-lg">
      <div class="max-w-full">
        <p class="typeset">
          I like to use Astro for most things, especially more static sites and
          blogs, and this is no exception. I've learned web tech primarily with
          React, and I think Astro, while not React, is familiar and comfortable
          to me.<br /> For similar reasons, I like to use TailwindCSS (it's nice
          to have css-in-code without the overhead of something like styled components).
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div
    class="mx-auto mt-4 grid max-w-screen-lg grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-12"
  >
    <div class="col-span-2 flex min-w-full flex-col">
      <div class="flex flex-row items-end gap-2 md:ml-auto">
        <p class="text-muted-foreground font-serif">Typography</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-span-8 min-w-full rounded-lg">
      <div class="max-w-full">
        <p class="typeset">
          Currently, this site is typed in Mi Sans and Sentient. Mi Sans is a
          font Xiaomi made for their MiOS operating system they use on their
          devices. I find that it works well for general body text, while
          looking a bit more expressive. Sentient is used for headings and
          display text. It's a distinctive, humanistic, and modern serif, much
          like Labor and Wait's <i>Copernicus</i>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div
    class="mx-auto mt-4 grid max-w-screen-lg grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-12"
  >
    <div class="col-span-2 flex min-w-full flex-col">
      <div class="flex flex-row items-end gap-2 md:ml-auto">
        <p class="text-muted-foreground font-serif">Colors</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-span-8 min-w-full rounded-lg">
      <div class="max-w-full">
        <p class="typeset">
          This site uses a theme based off Rosé Pine. The color palette features
          soft, muted tones inspired by the natural world, with gentler
          contrasts for readability. I like the slight pink tint of the whole
          theme, it reads to me as more inviting.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
